  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Publication of the Collected Works of Fr. Ricardo Falla SJ</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is to support the publication of Fr. Falla&apos;s collected research.

The civil war in Guatemala and the government and military repression leading up to it, claimed more than 200,000 civilian victims. Perhaps the best known chronicler of the wave of massacres, unleashed on the indigenous population, in the Western Highlands of Guatemala is anthropologist author and Jesuit priest Ricardo Falla; who, with the support of CAFOD, became the key witness and recorder of human rights violations.  Father Falla provided the information which fed into the research and campaigning work of Amnesty International during the 1980s and 1990s.  

In 2009 he was invited as a key witness to give his testimony to Judge Santiago Pedraz in Madrid who instituted the hearings in Spain, into the Guatemalan genocide. As a result the Guatemalan church and wider civil society, was able to press for the trial of former President General Efrain Rios Montt (which is currently taking place).</narrative>
  </description>
